# Minimal s=2 rigidity gate: Step 4b-1, exact class derivation — 2026-10-29

## Provenance

- **Charter:** [`MINIMAL_S2_RIGIDITY_GATE.md`](../theory/MINIMAL_S2_RIGIDITY_GATE.md),
  preregistration commit `785565c`.
- **Starting point:** stage (a), reviewed by Grok and promoted in `b67ea83`. It leaves five classes
  with a faithful projective action.
- **Authorization:** stage 4b-1 in `cfdc4a8` ("Autorizo 4b-1"). The user raised the budget from
  1 hour to 3 hours.
- **Timing:** started 13:06 UTC. The certificate passed at 13:13 UTC.
- **Certificate:** `scripts/verify_minimal_s2_step4b1.py`. The first version (`38f462c`,
  SHA-256 `5f91feaeece0d36a…`, 16/16) was reviewed by Astra
  ([review](../debates/2026-10-29--minimal-s2-step4b1-review-astra/informe_astra.md)). This
  repaired version (SHA-256 `5b0122f11df6f88d…`) runs 17/17 exact checks in about 110 s, Python
  3.12.3, SymPy 1.14.0. The repairs A-4B1-01..06 are listed at the end.
- **Full sweep:** 49/49 verifiers pass ([record](2026-10-29--minimal-s2-step4b1-run_all.tsv)),
  rerun after the repairs ([record](2026-10-29--minimal-s2-step4b1-repairs-run_all.tsv)).
- **Evidence level:** **PRELIMINARY**. First round of review (Astra) accepted the per-class
  results and requested six repairs, applied here; second round pending.

## Result

| Class (stage (a)) | Real parameters | Outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `(O)`, family F | 4 | `EMPTY_CLASS`: unit ideal, by both constructions |
| `(T, tetrahedron)`, family P | 8 | `EMPTY_CLASS`: unit ideal, by both constructions |
| `(D4)`, family F | 8 | `EMPTY_CLASS`: unit ideal, by both constructions |
| `(C4, face)`, family P | 16 | `EMPTY_CLASS`: unit ideal, by both constructions |
| `(V4, tetrahedron, Pauli)`, family P | 16 | `UNITARY_SYMBOLS_EXIST`. The ideal is not `(1)` (79 s). The explicit witness `U(q) = e^{-iq_x σ_x} e^{-iq_y σ_y} e^{-iq_z σ_z}` is a real point, checked in the certificate itself; the Pavia symbol of chirality 1 is a secondary control |

**Consequence.** In the frozen families (d=3, `N_3` without on-site term, `s=2`, proper cube
rotations, Eq. (2) not assumed), the only nonempty isotropy class is
`(V4, tetrahedron, Pauli)`: family P, `G = V4` (the three axial half-turns), `S_+` a tetrahedron,
`ρ` conjugate to the inclusion. Its group and representation coincide with P17's. The class is
not "P17 minus Eq. (2)" (charter, family P row, A-R1-03): it is the restriction to proper cube
rotations and an oriented four-generator presentation.
- The `C4` face class, the one where the general ceiling was not certified, is empty. Within the
  `C4` class the outcome `COUNTEREXAMPLE_VERIFIED_ABOVE` therefore has no object. In the
  surviving class it is still open: it depends on which nodes an admissible transport reaches
  (Step 4b-2).
- The `T` and `O` results match the step-01 `T2s`/`O2s` controls, which were anticipations
  there.

**Not decided here:**
- the dimension and components of the `(V4, Pauli)` class;
- whether every member satisfies Eq. (2) (Q-a);
- nodes, `c_0`, `c_strict^iso` (Step 4b-2, not authorized);
- Q-b (Step 4a, not authorized).

## Method

**Parametrization.**
- For a faithful class, `ρ: G → SO(3)` is conjugate to the inclusion. A constant basis change
  `W` absorbs the conjugation and preserves unitarity, so emptiness or existence for
  `ρ` = inclusion holds for the whole class.
- Write `T_h = a_h I + b_h·σ` with `a_h ∈ C` and `b_h ∈ C^3`. Conjugation by the spin-1/2 lift
  of `g` acts as `b ↦ g b`, `a ↦ a`, with `g` an integer signed permutation matrix. Covariance is
  `a_{gh} = a_h`, `b_{gh} = g b_h`. All group arithmetic is with integers.

**Two constructions of the covariant space, with shared infrastructure.**
- (i) Per orbit: the base coefficient is restricted to the fixed space of its stabilizer, and
  the orbit is filled by covariance. Well-definedness is checked.
- (ii) All eight `T_h` are free and covariance is imposed as linear equations for every
  `(g, h)`, then solved.

Both use the same group action (`S0.act`), the same `matvec`, the same Pauli basis and the same
unitarity generator. They can detect an error in the stabilizer/orbit filling of (i), but not an
error in that shared code.
- In the four empty classes both give the same number of real parameters and the unit ideal.
- In `(V4, Pauli)` construction (ii) is only compared by the number of real parameters (16). Its
  Groebner basis is not computed. Equal dimension does not prove that the two subspaces are
  equal.

**Unitarity.** The 27 coefficient identities, split into real and imaginary parts, use the
reviewed step-01 generator. The reduced Groebner basis is exact (grevlex). A basis equal to `[1]`
means no complex solution, and hence no real solution.

**Existence.** An ideal other than `(1)` is not taken as existence. The real point is the
explicit witness proposed in the Astra review:
`U(q) = e^{-iq_x σ_x} e^{-iq_y σ_y} e^{-iq_z σ_z}`, that is
`T_{(x,y,z)} = P_x^x P_y^y P_z^z` with `P_j^{±1} = (I ± σ_j)/2`. The certificate checks, without
imported code:
- all eight `T_h` are nonzero;
- Laurent unitarity in both orders, `Σ_{h'−h=ℓ} T_h^† T_{h'} = δ_{ℓ0} I` and
  `Σ_{h'−h=ℓ} T_{h'} T_h^† = δ_{ℓ0} I`, for every displacement `ℓ`;
- covariance `a_{gh} = a_h`, `b_{gh} = g b_h` for every `g ∈ V4` and `h ∈ N_3`.

Negative controls run during the repair: doubling one coefficient fails the unitarity check, and
the witness is not covariant under a `C4` generator. The reviewed Pavia symbol of chirality 1
passes the same covariance check as a secondary control; its unitarity comes from
`verify_irreducible_isotropy_step01.py`.

**DEP19 (A30), audit only.** It was read, but not used for any outcome.
- It is the general `s=2` BCC family only modulo relabelling of the generators, the PT map
  `A ↦ A^†`, basis change and the swap 2↔3. Several steps rest on "it is easy to see".
- (A30) keeps a free unitary `V`. DEP19's Eq. (14) is the normalization `Σ_h A_h = I_s`, not an
  isotropy condition, and (A32) does not by itself impose the Pauli covariance.
- Using (A30) as a cross-check of the `(V4, Pauli)` class remains to be done.

## Scope and limits

- **Frozen families only.** The emptiness results need all eight `T_h != 0` only through the
  frozen class definition; the unit ideal holds without that condition.
- **What `UNITARY_SYMBOLS_EXIST` covers.** It certifies one real point. It says nothing about the
  rest of the class, about Eq. (2) or about speeds.
- **Ceiling.** The surviving class contains the axial `D2`, so the general ceiling
  `c_0 <= c_strict^iso` applies there, at nodes reachable by an admissible transport.
- **No novelty claim.** The group and representation of `(V4, Pauli)` are P17's.

## Repairs after the Astra review (A-4B1-01..06)

| ID | Repair |
| --- | --- |
| A-4B1-01 (dependencies not attached) | Existence no longer rests on `S1`: the explicit witness is checked inside the certificate. `S1` is still used for the unitarity generator and Groebner call, and is attached to the second round. |
| A-4B1-02 (no Groebner for `V4` in construction (ii)) | Text corrected: only the parameter count is compared there. |
| A-4B1-03 (shared infrastructure) | Constructions described as sharing infrastructure, with what they can and cannot detect. |
| A-4B1-04 (identification with P17) | Class named exactly; coincidence of group and representation with P17 only. |
| A-4B1-05 (`..._ABOVE`) | Restricted to the `C4` class. |
| A-4B1-06 (DEP19 Eq. (14)) | Corrected: (14) is the normalization `Σ_h A_h = I_s`. |

Not adopted as a result here: Astra's argument that every active unitary symbol of the
`(V4, Pauli)` class satisfies Eq. (2). It is an anticipation for Q-a, decided in Step 4b-2 with a
certificate.

=== DOCUMENT 2: verify_minimal_s2_step4b1.py ===

"""Exact class derivation (Step 4b-1) of theory/MINIMAL_S2_RIGIDITY_GATE.md for the five faithful
classes left by stage (a) (reports/2026-10-29--minimal-s2-step00.md).

Parametrization (exact, no numerical group identification):
  For a faithful class, rho: G -> SO(3) is (up to SO(3) conjugation, absorbed by a constant basis
  change W) the inclusion G subset SO(3). Write T_h = a_h I + b_h . sigma with a_h in C, b_h in C^3.
  Conjugation by the spin-1/2 lift of g acts as b -> g b (g an integer signed permutation matrix),
  a -> a. Covariance T_{gh} = R_g T_h R_g^dagger is then a_{gh} = a_h, b_{gh} = g b_h. Per G-orbit
  of N_3, the base coefficient b_{h0} is restricted to the fixed space of Stab(h0), and the orbit
  is filled by covariance (well-definedness is checked).

Per class it computes the reduced Groebner basis (grevlex, exact) of the real unitarity system.
  basis == [1]   -> EMPTY_CLASS (no complex, hence no real, solution);
  otherwise      -> a real point is sought: the explicit witness
                    U(q) = exp(-i q_x sigma_x) exp(-i q_y sigma_y) exp(-i q_z sigma_z), i.e.
                    T_(x,y,z) = P_x^x P_y^y P_z^z with P_j^(+-1) = (I +- sigma_j)/2 (proposed by the
                    Astra review of 4b-1), whose covariance, eight nonzero coefficients and
                    Laurent unitarity are checked here without imported code; if it lies in the
                    class -> UNITARY_SYMBOLS_EXIST; else OPEN_AFTER_CLASS_DERIVATION (an ideal
                    different from (1) is not existence). The reviewed Pavia symbol is kept as a
                    secondary control (it relies on the step-01 certificate).
A per-class time limit implements the stage budget; a timeout gives OPEN_AFTER_CLASS_DERIVATION.

What it does NOT certify: completeness of the dimension/components of nonempty classes, nodes,
c_0, c_strict^iso, Q-a, or anything about DEP19 (A30), which is only an external cross-check.
"""

import itertools
import signal
import sys
import time

import sympy as sp

sys.path.insert(0, "scripts")
import verify_minimal_s2_step00 as S0  # this charter's stage (a) certificate, read-only
import verify_irreducible_isotropy_step01 as S1  # reviewed helpers, read-only
from certificate_utils import sym_zero

CHECKS = 0
I = sp.I
PAULI = [sp.Matrix([[0, 1], [1, 0]]), sp.Matrix([[0, -I], [I, 0]]), sp.Matrix([[1, 0], [0, -1]])]
N3 = S0.N3
LIMIT = int(sys.argv[sys.argv.index("--limit") + 1]) if "--limit" in sys.argv else 600


def require(cond, label):
    global CHECKS
    if not cond:
        print(f"[FAIL] {label}")
        raise SystemExit(1)
    CHECKS += 1
    print(f"[PASS] {label}", flush=True)


def matvec(M, v):
    return [sum(M[i][k] * v[k] for k in range(3)) for i in range(3)]


def class_symbol(G, tag):
    """Covariant symbol with rho = inclusion; returns (T, real params)."""
    T, params = {}, []
    for oi, orb in enumerate(S0.orbits(G, N3)):
        h0 = min(orb)
        stab = [g for g in G if S0.act(g, h0) == h0]
        a = sp.symbols(f"a{oi}_r a{oi}_i", real=True)
        bs = sp.symbols(f"b{oi}_0:6", real=True)
        b = [bs[2 * j] + I * bs[2 * j + 1] for j in range(3)]
        # fixed space of Stab(h0): g b = b for all g in stab (real linear conditions on Re, Im)
        eqs = []
        for g in stab:
            gb = matvec(g, b)
            eqs += [sp.re(gb[j] - b[j]) for j in range(3)] + [sp.im(gb[j] - b[j]) for j in range(3)]
        sol = sp.solve([e for e in eqs if e != 0], bs, dict=True) if any(e != 0 for e in eqs) else [{}]
        sol = sol[0]
        b = [sp.expand(x.subs(sol)) for x in b]
        free = sorted(set().union(*[sp.sympify(x).free_symbols for x in b]) | set(a), key=str)
        params += free
        base = (a[0] + I * a[1]) * sp.eye(2) + sum((b[j] * PAULI[j] for j in range(3)), sp.zeros(2))
        for g in G:
            h = S0.act(g, h0)
            gb = matvec(g, b)
            Th = (a[0] + I * a[1]) * sp.eye(2) + sum((gb[j] * PAULI[j] for j in range(3)), sp.zeros(2))
            if h in T:
                if not sym_zero(T[h] - Th):
                    raise AssertionError(f"{tag}: ill-defined orbit map")
            else:
                T[h] = sp.expand(Th)
    return T, params


def class_symbol_linear(G, tag):
    """Second construction: all eight T_h free (a_h, b_h), covariance imposed as linear equations
    a_{gh} = a_h, b_{gh} = g b_h for every g in G and h in N_3, then solved."""
    vars_, T, eqs = [], {}, []
    coef = {}
    for k, h in enumerate(N3):
        xs = sp.symbols(f"y{k}_0:8", real=True)
        vars_ += list(xs)
        coef[h] = ([xs[0] + I * xs[1]], [xs[2 + 2 * j] + I * xs[3 + 2 * j] for j in range(3)])
    for g in G:
        for h in N3:
            a, b = coef[h]
            a2, b2 = coef[S0.act(g, h)]
            gb = matvec(g, b)
            for d in [a2[0] - a[0]] + [b2[j] - gb[j] for j in range(3)]:
                eqs += [sp.re(d), sp.im(d)]
    sol = sp.solve([e for e in eqs if e != 0], vars_, dict=True)[0]
    for h in N3:
        a, b = coef[h]
        T[h] = sp.expand(((a[0] * sp.eye(2) + sum((b[j] * PAULI[j] for j in range(3)),
                                                   sp.zeros(2)))).subs(sol))
    params = sorted(set().union(*[M.free_symbols for M in T.values()]), key=str)
    return T, params


class Timeout(Exception):
    pass


def _alarm(signum, frame):
    raise Timeout


def witness_symbol():
    """Explicit witness T_(x,y,z) = P_x^x P_y^y P_z^z, P_j^(+-1) = (I +- sigma_j)/2."""
    P = {(j, e): (sp.eye(2) + e * PAULI[j]) / 2 for j in range(3) for e in (1, -1)}
    return {h: sp.expand(P[(0, h[0])] * P[(1, h[1])] * P[(2, h[2])]) for h in N3}


def laurent_unitary(T):
    """sum_{h'-h=l} T_h^dagger T_h' = delta_{l0} I and sum_{h'-h=l} T_h' T_h^dagger = delta_{l0} I,
    exactly, for every displacement l (both U^dagger U = I and U U^dagger = I)."""
    diffs = {}
    for h in N3:
        for hp in N3:
            diffs.setdefault(tuple(a - b for a, b in zip(hp, h)), []).append((h, hp))
    for ell, pairs in diffs.items():
        target = sp.eye(2) if ell == (0, 0, 0) else sp.zeros(2)
        A = sum((T[h].H * T[hp] for h, hp in pairs), sp.zeros(2))
        B = sum((T[hp] * T[h].H for h, hp in pairs), sp.zeros(2))
        if not (sym_zero(A - target) and sym_zero(B - target)):
            return False
    return True


def covariant(T, G):
    """a_{gh} = a_h and b_{gh} = g b_h for every g in G and h in N_3 (rho = inclusion)."""
    def coeffs(X):
        return [sp.expand((X * P).trace() / 2) for P in PAULI]
    return all(sym_zero(sp.Matrix(coeffs(T[S0.act(g, h)])) - sp.Matrix(matvec(g, coeffs(T[h]))))
               and sym_zero(T[S0.act(g, h)].trace() - T[h].trace())
               for g in G for h in N3)


def pavia_point(G):
    """Return a Pavia chirality covariant under G with rho = inclusion, or None."""
    z = sp.symbols("z1:4")
    for ch in (1, -1):
        M, _ = S1.WD.published_symbol(3, ch, z)
        T2 = {}
        for v in N3:
            mono = sp.prod([zi ** (vi + 1) for zi, vi in zip(z, v)])
            T2[tuple(-x for x in v)] = M.applyfunc(
                lambda e: sp.Poly(sp.expand(e * sp.prod(z)), *z).coeff_monomial(mono))
        def coeffs(X):
            return [sp.simplify((X * P).trace() / 2) for P in PAULI]
        ok = all(sym_zero(sp.Matrix(coeffs(T2[S0.act(g, h)])) -
                          sp.Matrix(matvec(g, coeffs(T2[h]))))
                 and sym_zero(T2[S0.act(g, h)].trace() - T2[h].trace())
                 for g in G for h in N3)
        if ok:
            return ch
    return None


def main():
    t0 = time.time()
    classesP = []
    subs = {S0.closure([a, b]) for a in S0.O for b in S0.O}
    pairs_pm = [(v, tuple(-x for x in v)) for v in N3 if v[0] == 1]
    choices = [frozenset(c) for c in itertools.product(*pairs_pm)]
    for G in subs:
        for S in choices:
            if (all(S0.act(g, v) in S for g in G for v in S) and len(S0.orbits(G, S)) == 1
                    and not any(any(S0.conj(g, G) == H and frozenset(S0.act(g, v) for v in S) == Tt
                                    for g in S0.O) for H, Tt in classesP)):
                classesP.append((G, S))
    classesF = []
    for G in subs:
        if len(S0.orbits(G, N3)) == 1 and not any(any(S0.conj(g, G) == H for g in S0.O)
                                                  for H in classesF):
            classesF.append(G)
    named = {}
    for G, S in classesP:
        named[{(4, "tetrahedron"): "V4_tet_Pauli", (12, "tetrahedron"): "T_tet",
               (4, "face"): "C4_face"}[(len(G), S0.kind(S))]] = G
    for G in classesF:
        named[{8: "D4", 24: "O"}[len(G)]] = G
    require(sorted(named) == ["C4_face", "D4", "O", "T_tet", "V4_tet_Pauli"],
            "the five faithful classes of stage (a) are reconstructed (families P and F)")

    results = {}
    signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, _alarm)
    for name in ("O", "T_tet", "D4", "C4_face", "V4_tet_Pauli"):
        G = named[name]
        T, params = class_symbol(G, name)
        require(len(T) == 8, f"{name}: covariant symbol defined on all of N_3, "
                f"{len(params)} real parameters")
        eqs = S1.unitarity_equations(T, 2)
        t1 = time.time()
        signal.alarm(LIMIT)
        try:
            unit = S1.groebner_is_unit(eqs, params)
            signal.alarm(0)
        except Timeout:
            results[name] = f"OPEN_AFTER_CLASS_DERIVATION (Groebner timeout {LIMIT} s)"
            print(f"      {name}: {results[name]}", flush=True)
            continue
        if unit:
            results[name] = "EMPTY_CLASS"
            require(True, f"{name}: unitarity ideal is (1) -> EMPTY_CLASS "
                    f"({time.time() - t1:.0f} s)")
            # second construction (linear covariance on free T_h), must agree
            T2, p2 = class_symbol_linear(G, name)
            signal.alarm(LIMIT)
            try:
                unit2 = S1.groebner_is_unit(S1.unitarity_equations(T2, 2), p2)
                signal.alarm(0)
            except Timeout:
                unit2 = None
            require(unit2 is True and len(p2) == len(params),
                    f"{name}: second construction (linear covariance on free T_h, {len(p2)} real "
                    "parameters) also gives the unit ideal")
        else:
            T2, p2 = class_symbol_linear(G, name)
            require(len(p2) == len(params),
                    f"{name}: second construction has the same number of real parameters "
                    f"({len(p2)})")
            W = witness_symbol()
            ok = (all(not sym_zero(W[h]) for h in N3) and laurent_unitary(W) and covariant(W, G))
            results[name] = ("UNITARY_SYMBOLS_EXIST (explicit witness)" if ok
                             else "OPEN_AFTER_CLASS_DERIVATION (ideal != (1), no certified real point)")
            print(f"      {name}: ideal != (1) ({time.time() - t1:.0f} s); {results[name]}", flush=True)
            require(ok, f"{name}: explicit witness exp(-iq_x s_x) exp(-iq_y s_y) exp(-iq_z s_z) has "
                    "eight nonzero coefficients, is Laurent-unitary and covariant with rho = "
                    "inclusion (checked here, no imported code)")
            ch = pavia_point(G)
            require(ch == 1, f"{name}: secondary control, Pavia chirality {ch} is also covariant "
                    "with rho = inclusion (unitarity from the step-01 certificate)")
    print(f"      results: {results}")
    print(f"VERDICT: {CHECKS}/{CHECKS} exact checks passed in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s. "
          f"Per class: {results}")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()

